<!--
  The morning pre-flight check, run by launchd.

  It runs agent/preflight.py at 09:00, half an hour before the market opens, and
  checks that everything the trading day needs is actually working before the day
  starts. If any check fails it writes /Users/mtalib/workspace_repos/personal_repo/agentic_trading/output/NO_TRADE_TODAY, and the loop
  reads that file and refuses to open new positions for the rest of the day. So a
  bad morning stops the day rather than trading through it.

  It places no orders. All it does is read things and run the scanner, which is
  why it gets a ten minute timeout: the scanner on its own can take four minutes.

  Worth knowing: if the Mac is asleep at 09:00, launchd runs the job once when it
  wakes up, and there is no setting here that turns that off. A pre-flight that
  lands at 11:00 is late but not wrong, and it still writes NO_TRADE_TODAY if
  something is broken.
-->
